{"type":"message","id":"cab293ea","parentId":"6c358402","timestamp":"2026-03-09T08:16:39.730Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7d7d58de7a5b4db19279580d","toolName":"glob","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"durationMs\": 15,\n  \"numFiles\": 0,\n  \"filenames\": [],\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}],"details":{"durationMs":15,"numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"truncated":false},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773044199727}}
{"type":"message","id":"bfc98f50","parentId":"cab293ea","timestamp":"2026-03-09T08:16:39.741Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0714466e614544f28784b920","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 2026-03-08 Session Memory\n\n## Bug Fixes\n\n### Metrics Queue Database Corruption\n- **Issue**: Metrics queue repeatedly failing with \"Failed to flush metrics\" errors\n- **Root Cause**: SQLite database corruption - \"database disk image is malformed\" in `~/.openclaw/reasoning.db`\n- **Symptoms**: Logs show database corruption detection, failed recovery attempts, tool-analytics-olap errors\n- **Solution**: Delete corrupted `~/.openclaw/reasoning.db` and restart gateway\n- **Impact**: Non-critical metrics only, safe to delete without data loss\n- **Verification**: After restart, logs show \"Metrics database initialized\" with no errors\n- **Code Changes**: Enhanced error logging in metrics-queue.ts to show actual error details (previously empty)\n\n## System Health\n\n### Working Systems (Post-Fix)\n- ✅ Metrics queue (reasoning.db recreated successfully)\n- ✅ Meta-cognitive engine (reflection timer running, 360min interval)\n- ✅ Reasoning tracker initialized\n- ✅ Predictive integration (OLAP, analytics, RL selector)\n- ✅ Event mesh persistence\n\n## Ongoing Projects\n\n### LinkedIn Growth Plan (Z.E Digital Tech)\n- **Started**: 2026-02-28\n- **Goal**: 2 → 500+ followers in 6 months\n- **Status**: Daily engagement reminders active (8am, 2pm, 6pm weekdays)\n- **Next**: Sunday analytics review scheduled (today)\n- **File**: memory/linkedin-growth-plan.md\n\n### X/Twitter Growth (@zedigitaltech)\n- **Started**: 2026-03-07\n- **Current**: 2 followers, ~55 following, 22+ posts\n- **Progress**: Posted 4/5 tweets, followed 2 accounts (browser issues)\n- **Next**: Need 35+ follows, 50 likes, 20 replies, tweet #5\n- **Browser**: CDP available on port 9222 (eloclaw profile)\n- **File**: memory/x-growth-strategy-2026-03-07.md\n\n## Completed Implementations\n\n### Event Partitioning System\n- **Status**: ✅ COMPLETE (2026-03-08)\n- **Files Created**:\n  - `src/infra/event-partition-manager.ts` - Partition manager with all 9 critical fixes\n  - `src/infra/event-partition-manager.test.ts` - Comprehensive test suite\n  - Modified `src/agents/event-mesh.ts` - Integrated partition routing\n- **Fixes Implemented**:\n  1. ✅ SQL injection prevention (partition name validation)\n  2. ✅ UTC timezone consistency\n  3. ✅ Timestamp validation (seconds vs milliseconds detection)\n  4. ✅ Id-based cursor pagination (no OFFSET race conditions)\n  5. ✅ Proper transaction usage\n  6. ✅ Backup + verification + rollback capability\n  7. ✅ Initialization guards (prevent race conditions)\n  8. ✅ Partition-aware queries\n  9. ✅ WAL mode for better concurrency\n- **Expected Improvement**: 10x faster queries on large event tables, automatic old data cleanup\n- **Migration**: Automatic one-time migration from legacy `agent_events` table\n\n---\n\n*Session notes for continuity across compaction cycles*\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773044199738}}
